# expect: is declared `text` but is given a number
# An annotation on a local is not decoration - it is what tells the compiler an
# element type it cannot infer, which is the only way to read a list out of a
# list (`r: list of number = rs[i]`). Something load-bearing may not also be
# unchecked: this compiled in silence and printed 5.
#
# Only LITERALS are judged. Anywhere else the value's own type may be a guess,
# and there the annotation is the one being believed on purpose - erroring on a
# disagreement would forbid the use that makes annotations worth having.
define main() -> number:
    x: text = 5
    print_line(x)
    0
